Dānā is an agentic CAD and manufacturing engineer. Read ARCHITECTURE.md before changing anything; it is the current ground truth.

Hard constraints — never break these:
1. 8 GB VRAM (RTX 2080): keep ollama_num_ctx() <= 8192, llm_lock serialization for local Ollama, keep_alive 0 on socket close. OCR, TTS and tool retrieval (384-d hash embeddings) stay on CPU. No neural embedding models, no persistent GPU daemons, no torch in requirements.txt.
2. Token budget: never replay full chat history (system + user message + working_memory.summary <= 1,200 chars). Keep _TOOL_TOKEN_BUDGET = 2000, _MAX_ACTIVE_TOOLS = 30, schema_minify, capability decay, lazy tool discovery, one tool per LLM step, and the planning/executing FSM gates.
3. FreeCAD: one FreeCADCmd subprocess per call through _run_freecad_script (_RUN_ONCE_WRAPPER, .FCStd.bak rollback), one Session_Active.FCStd per session, objects resolved by name. New CAD operations go into the Universal CAD IR (dana/plugins/freecad/ir.py + universal_ir.py.jinja2) so live execution, macro export and the parametric rebuild stay identical.
4. DANA_HEADLESS=true is the default safety lock; never unset it in tests. Keep the trimesh mock engine working (CI and the Hugging Face Space use it).
5. Approvals, auto_approve and API keys are never persisted. execute_freecad_script, modify_existing_freecad_document and dispatch_to_printer always require approval.

Before committing: pytest (DANA_HEADLESS=true DANA_OS_DRY_RUN=1), scripts/ci/check_boundaries.py, scripts/ci/check_dead_code_incremental.py, and `npm run build` in frontend/. Commit with explicit pathspecs (git commit -- <files>).
